From: yzddmr6 <46088090+yzddmr6@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] tests: expect an empty error reply for an unsupported registry method

The imported listener change answers unsupported methods with an empty reply
instead of terminating the transport. Update the existing liuqin ROM registry
regression to require that error and free its reply. The strict scalar guard
and the property allowlist assertions remain unchanged.

License: same as the existing liuqin hexagonrpc registry test.

--- a/tests/test_sns_registry.c
+++ b/tests/test_sns_registry.c
@@ -195,8 +195,10 @@
 	sc = REMOTE_SCALARS_MAKE(1, 2, 1);
 	result = invoke_property(property0, PROPERTY_VALUE_MAX, sc,
 				 &dispatch_ret, &returned);
-	if (!dispatch_ret || result != AEE_EUNSUPPORTED || returned != NULL)
-		fail("method 1 was not rejected by the one-method interface");
+	if (dispatch_ret || result != AEE_EUNSUPPORTED || returned == NULL
+	 || returned[0].s != 0 || returned[0].p != NULL)
+		fail("method 1 did not receive an empty unsupported reply");
+	iobuf_free(1, returned);
 
 	sc = REMOTE_SCALARS_MAKE(0, 2, 2);
 	result = invoke_property(property0, PROPERTY_VALUE_MAX, sc,
